{"c":[{"id":"89b95b00905689c6","sum":"A18-I3: Cotypist takes plain Tab on Sam's Mac (otherTabOwners lists it); KeyType silences most mid-line ghost candidates and SuffixFit scores the first token only; memory.ndjson is the helper's golden, lines by id; paste refused over unrestorable clipboard types.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e08d1ae5c480f911","sum":"A18: Cotypist on Sam's Mac takes plain Tab one word at a time (debug state lists otherTabOwners); mid-line ghost text is mostly silenced by KeyType's lowConfidenceMidLine, and SuffixFit scores only the first token after the caret (floor -7.0 nats).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T183212Z-37e231b8935fe92e","text":"Cotypist runs on Sam's Mac with its accept-partial shortcut on plain Tab (one word per press): Q1's one-word Tabs were Cotypist's, Caret's tap.consumed/offers.claimed truly 0; debug state lists otherTabOwners (A18).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T183212Z-d8342f2456ba377e","text":"Ghost text between words: KeyType's lowConfidenceMidLine silences most mid-line candidates in Caret --probe-replay; A18's SuffixFit scores only the first token after the caret (floor -7.0 nats, dev-run-3), since tokens 2-3 were near 0 for every candidate.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"88019d610c5e4bca","sum":"I3: Fixtures/memory.ndjson is the helper's golden byte for byte (wrote line is host-memory-9); tests find lines by id; the host refuses the paste route when the clipboard holds a type it cannot restore (file URL, private types), writing by AX instead.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T195224Z-8ef6ab64ee3f2dea","text":"I3: apps/caret Fixtures/memory.ndjson is the helper's golden byte for byte as of H1 (host-memory-5 request added, A16's wrote line is host-memory-9, no -8); tests find lines by id, never by index.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T195224Z-99ff86984f364892","text":"I3: host refuses the paste route when the prior clipboard holds a type outside ReconcilingClipboard.restorableTypes (file URL, private types): AX write instead, else fail clipboardUnrestorable. A17's VM probe lost a file-url item 5/5 while restore said restored.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c539feeaf5360a4d","sum":"W3-M1: XPC code-signing requirement guards what a client receives, so XPCHostLink sends nothing before a verified reply; memory markdown lives in <dir>/Memory and grants no authority (permissions stay in sqlite); write U+2028 as an escape in regexes.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"569740c12f8fdab5","sum":"W3: client setCodeSigningRequirement blocks what it receives, not its first call; XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply. Memory is markdown: MemoryStore(dir) uses <dir>/Memory; main.ts uses the real folder only without --data-dir.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204321Z-a08d2817ff5ece3d","text":"W3: NSXPCConnection.setCodeSigningRequirement on the client blocks what it receives, not its own first call; whoever owns the Mach name sees open's arguments, so XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204904Z-98cc6d5ebfceb30a","text":"Personal memory is markdown (helper/src/memory): MemoryStore(dir) keeps it in <dir>/Memory unless told otherwise, and main.ts uses ~/Library/Application Support/Caret/Memory only when --data-dir is not given, so tests and evals never open the real folder.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6e639a4926698b7e","sum":"Memory markdown grants no authority (permissions, onItsOwn, clean runs stay in memory.sqlite; editing a skill file puts it back on Tab; fileDigest catches offline edits). vite's oxc rejects a raw U+2028/U+2029 in a regex literal: write the escape.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204920Z-024f4219fb18c6cf","text":"Memory markdown grants no authority: permissions and a skill's onItsOwn, clean runs and hand-off stay in memory.sqlite; editing a skill's file puts it back on Tab, and SkillJson.fileDigest catches edits made while Caret was stopped.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204920Z-0ba29fff62387456","text":"vite's oxc parser rejects a regex literal holding a raw U+2028/U+2029 (a line terminator); write the \\u2028 escape. An agent's Write tool can turn the escape into the raw character.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
